From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:35:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Default the alter entry data's lookup mode

The PEG transformer builds many alter infos from a default-constructed
AlterEntryData, whose if_not_found member nothing sets, and passes it
by value, so GCC 15 reports the member read uninitialized in the copy
that passing by value makes. A default in the declaration gives the
temporary a value. Upstream later passes the data by reference, after
which no caller copies the temporary.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/parser/parsed_data/alter_info.hpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/parser/parsed_data/alter_info.hpp b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/parser/parsed_data/alter_info.hpp
index 5ba8680fc9..c90bdf1283 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/parser/parsed_data/alter_info.hpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/parser/parsed_data/alter_info.hpp
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ struct AlterEntryData {
 	string catalog;
 	string schema;
 	string name;
-	OnEntryNotFound if_not_found;
+	OnEntryNotFound if_not_found = OnEntryNotFound::THROW_EXCEPTION;
 };
 
 struct AlterInfo : public ParseInfo {
